<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002-TAUTOLOGICAL-DUPLICATE-CHECK>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI11-QA7-ARCH-002-TAUTOLOGICAL-DUPLICATE-CHECK" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T12:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Duplicate-router and adapter-storage/nudge checks are each scoped to a single already-known file" ;
  triage:description "Two sub-checks inside fn ai11_deletion_gate_rejects_retired_windows_transport_ast_and_dependencies() (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs, commit bb20fd9a on feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation, PR #607) share the same narrow-scope defect. (a) The duplicate-router check does `dispatcher_source.matches(\"impl ApiRouter for\").count()` against exactly one hardcoded file, crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs (`dispatcher_source`), so the count is tautologically always 1 regardless of whether a duplicate ApiRouter impl is added anywhere else in the workspace -- it can never actually detect a duplicate. (b) The adapter storage/nudge-call check (forbidden list: LocalServiceRuntime, persist_message, emit_post_send_effects, write_mail_with_runtime) only scans `local_tcp_source` (crates/atm-daemon/src/local_tcp_transport.rs, the Windows loopback-TCP adapter) -- one of three production transport adapters in crates/atm-daemon/src. The other two, local_ipc_transport.rs (Unix UDS) and https_transport.rs (cross-host HTTPS), are never scanned for storage/nudge-call violations. No active production violation exists today for either sub-check -- the risk is purely the gate's ability to catch a FUTURE regression." ;
  triage:category "boundary-gate-weakness" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T12:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002/s11/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002/s11/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002/s11/3> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002/s11/4> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/bb20fd9a> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s12/b6466aa1> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/bb20fd9a> ;
  triage:highestFixedBranch "feature/pAI-s12-post-write-router" ;
  triage:notes "RESOLUTION (2026-07-22 sweep): both sub-checks verifiably fixed on current integrate/phase-AI. (a) The adapter storage/nudge scan now iterates adapter_sources = [local TCP, local IPC, peer HTTPS] rather than only local_tcp_source (boundary_enforcement.rs ~line 423-439). (b) The duplicate-router check now sums production_api_router_implementation_count(path) across ai11_guarded_workspace_sources(&root) rather than matching a single hardcoded dispatcher file (~line 442-449). Cross-referenced with sibling finding AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST.ttl (same cwin fast-follow batch, PR #607), already recorded fixed on feature/pAI-s12-post-write-router (b6466aa1); this finding's fix landed in the same batch." .

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002-TAUTOLOGICAL-DUPLICATE-CHECK>
  triage:assignedTo "cwin" ;
  triage:dispatchChannel "direct-paste-non-atm" ;
  triage:notes "ASSIGNMENT UPDATE (team-lead, 2026-07-22): the AI.11 QA-7 fast-follow batch (this finding plus AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE and AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST) was reassigned from arch-ctm to cwin. Original ATM dispatch was message 01KY5PZ9PCJMZP3ZFA92NGCGS5 (task id AI11-QA7-FASTFOLLOW-DELETION-GATE-SCOPE, sent to arch-ctm). arch-ctm was subsequently stood down from this batch via ATM message 01KY5S0ZFQCPA89KD5WTM0Z6CA. cwin has no ATM identity, so the reassignment dispatch to cwin was delivered by direct-paste outside the ATM channel and left no ATM message trail on cwin's side; the stand-down message to arch-ctm is the only ATM-side record of the handoff. This note is the canonical audit trail for the reassignment." .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ARCH-002/s11/1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs" ;
  triage:line 1202 ;
  triage:snippet "let adapter_sources = [(\"local TCP\", read_source(&local_tcp)), (\"peer HTTPS\", read_source(&peer_https)),];" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closureNote "quality-mgr: verified against integrate/phase-AI head (efe73e1c) -- adapter storage/nudge scan now iterates over adapter_sources array (local TCP and peer HTTPS) instead of single hardcoded local_tcp file. Check applied uniformly to both adapters. Defect resolved. Stale occurrence from superseded branch feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation; closing to match reality. (2026-07-26)" ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation" ;
  triage:headSha "bb20fd9a" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/bb20fd9a> .

